WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.210
JAMIE: I contain multitudes.

00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:04.978
ALEX: Okay, but here's what I'm
genuinely curious about.

00:00:04.978 --> 00:00:07.565
ALEX: For someone who is
evaluating AI infrastructure right

00:00:07.565 --> 00:00:10.153
ALEX: now — say you're running a
mid-size company

00:00:10.153 --> 00:00:12.740
ALEX: with a real agentic use case
you're trying

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:15.328
ALEX: to build — does this change
your calculus?

00:00:15.413 --> 00:00:17.688
RUFUS: Possibly. If you've been
holding off on committing

00:00:17.688 --> 00:00:19.963
RUFUS: to a hardware vendor
because you didn't want

00:00:19.963 --> 00:00:22.238
RUFUS: to be entirely at the mercy
of cloud

00:00:22.238 --> 00:00:24.514
RUFUS: pricing, this gives you
another option to evaluate.

00:00:24.514 --> 00:00:26.789
RUFUS: It's not Nvidia-versus-
Google yet. But it's the clearest

00:00:26.789 --> 00:00:29.064
RUFUS: signal that Google wants to
be in that

00:00:29.064 --> 00:00:31.339
RUFUS: conversation.
